# What must never reach a build context.
#
# Two reasons. Secrets: a .env copied into a layer is a key in the image
# whatever the Dockerfile does afterwards. And the journal — it is the
# platform's state, it belongs in a volume, and baking one into an image
# means a redeploy quietly reverts every balance to whenever that image was
# built.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# The database, such as it is.
gateway/journal/
gateway/*.jnl
**/users.json

# Build output, which the build makes for itself.
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

.git/
.github/
design/
docs/
**/*.md
!README.md
